WEBVTT

00:10:30.162 --> 00:10:32.496
and there's been a mixed
response as to what

00:10:32.496 --> 00:10:34.246
the effects of those rules might be.

00:10:34.871 --> 00:10:36.704
Some people think it's going
to make a huge difference.

00:10:36.704 --> 00:10:39.496
Some people think it doesn't go far enough
and some people are angry about it,

00:10:39.787 --> 00:10:43.162
frankly. And you have really publicly
said that you think that

00:10:43.162 --> 00:10:45.829
the new rules are a good start
and you're optimistic.

00:10:46.121 --> 00:10:47.954
I'm curious, though, if you think
they're going to make

00:10:47.954 --> 00:10:51.204
a real tangible difference in the kinds
of movies that are getting produced.

00:10:51.371 --> 00:10:55.329
But again, because of the way in which the
sort of thresholds are structured,

00:10:55.996 --> 00:10:58.829
if you just hire one like
a woman of color in

00:10:58.829 --> 00:11:01.537
a senior role at your distribution
company and like have